                    {
                        "form_id": "1532a60f-793a-46bb-8e3d-4b857968d17e",
                        "entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "пета́рдах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d2712c0-a339-30d7-ad68-35376adbc824",
                        "entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор., воен. разрывной снаряд в виде металлического сосуда, наполненного порохом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b021203a-8578-4f0d-9646-52d53aa8422a",
                                "sense_id": "9d2712c0-a339-30d7-ad68-35376adbc824",
                                "text": "Кавалер Новодворский сделал пролом в переднем городке и дошел до самых Арбатских ворот, но здесь, прикладывая к ним петарду, был ранен в руку из мушкета."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c7627186-c38c-336f-a8a2-9f07eada72b0",
                        "entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор., техн. хлопушка, укладываемая на рельсы для сигнализирования требования немедленной остановки поезда"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "339fc155-4a09-4f77-acaf-c44022f98c1b",
                                "sense_id": "c7627186-c38c-336f-a8a2-9f07eada72b0",
                                "text": "Какой-то шутник решил устроить на улице переполох и доставши где-то петарду, употребляемую на линиях железных дорог для быстрой остановки поездов, положил её на рельсы конки перед самым проездом вагона."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f83acd9f-39f3-37c9-b872-5872c523c5ad",
                        "entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "взрывное пиротехническое изделие небольшой мощности в виде бумажной или картонной гильзы, наполненной пиротехническим составом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53040ffe-8778-420a-a582-58825b83eb45",
                                "sense_id": "f83acd9f-39f3-37c9-b872-5872c523c5ad",
                                "text": "Главный новогодний ритуал заключается в отпугивании злых духов. Для этого взрывают петарды, пистоны, запускают ракеты."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16353f94-5477-4c56-9578-0f311d9fdd06",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
                        "source_sense_description": "разрывной снаряд в виде металлического сосуда, наполненного порохом",
                        "target_lang_word": "petard",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "petard",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20b74c45-2ec3-36ef-8597-610f25ebe9fe",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb2c53c-7239-3e5b-8ffb-a06d81a0e363",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small, hat-shaped explosive device, used to breach a door or wall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0066c1de-dd37-4f3a-8fad-148cd6291044",
                                                "sense_id": "20b74c45-2ec3-36ef-8597-610f25ebe9fe",
                                                "text": "For tis the ſport to haue the enginer / Hoiſt with his ovvne petar, an't ſhall goe hard / But I vvill delue one yard belovve their mines, / And blovve them at the Moone: […]",
                                                "translation": "For it's amusing to have the engineer / Hoisted into the sky with his own explosive, and if I'm lucky / I will dig one yard below their mines, / And blow them towards the Moon: […]",
                                                "english": "For it's amusing to have the engineer / Hoisted into the sky with his own explosive, and if I'm lucky / I will dig one yard below their mines, / And blow them towards the Moon: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77da01db-e7a6-4d67-98da-cb92b1b0a957",
                                                "sense_id": "20b74c45-2ec3-36ef-8597-610f25ebe9fe",
                                                "text": "[…] Pipes, who acted as the enemy's forlorn hope, advanced to the gate with great intrepidity, and clapping his foot to the door, which was none of the ſtouteſt, with the execution and diſpatch of a petard, ſplit it into a thouſand pieces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3595d09-50ca-3230-9bd3-5d2aaeeb5239",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb2c53c-7239-3e5b-8ffb-a06d81a0e363",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything potentially explosive, in a non-literal sense."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5094033-fb3e-3191-96ac-af7c7e289084",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb2c53c-7239-3e5b-8ffb-a06d81a0e363",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A loud firecracker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "petard",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f21ae0af-744a-38dd-bac0-3c8803efb388",
                                        "entry_id": "c3092773-a7fe-373c-ad72-79d90fdae5a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To attack or blow a hole in (something) with a petard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0a5debb-1388-4554-bcf3-dc04635cdcb6",
                                                "sense_id": "f21ae0af-744a-38dd-bac0-3c8803efb388",
                                                "text": "The Souldier, if he but go to beſiege a cottage, to ſcale a Caſtle, to robbe a Church, to Pettard [translating petarder] a gate, to force a religious houſe, or any villenous act, before he attempt-it, praieth to God for his aſſiſtance, though his intents and hopes be full-fraught with crueltie, murther, couetiſe, luxurie, ſacriledge and all iniquitie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4736cffa-68f4-45fd-8cdb-b79a70ef4b21",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f4ecf60-b52b-391c-aa1e-dd5f514534a5",
